---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SupportFlow from '../components/SupportFlow.astro';
import TravelGuide from '../components/TravelGuide.astro';
import Mechanism from '../components/Mechanism.astro';

---
<Base description="Save a moderator's reply. ThreadSherpa watches your Discord forum, answers similar questions using saved replies, and links the original answer.">
  <TravelGuide />
  <section class="intro" id="top" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <canvas class="thread-field" data-thread-field aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="wrap intro__inner">

      <h1 id="intro-title"><span class="hero-line" data-hero-line>Give your support{' '}</span><span class="hero-line hero-line--second" data-hero-line>channel a break<span class="hero-period">.</span></span></h1>
      <div class="intro__bottom"><p data-hero-copy>Save a moderator’s reply.<br />ThreadSherpa uses it to answer similar questions in your Discord forum.</p><a class="scroll-cue" href="#how-it-works"><span>How it works</span><span class="scroll-cue__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <div class="guide-stop intro-guide-stop" data-guide-stop="intro" data-guide-pose="sleep" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <SupportFlow />

  <Mechanism />

  <section class="limits-section wrap" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div data-reveal><h2 id="limits-title">Limitations.</h2><div class="guide-stop limits-guide-stop" data-guide-stop="limits" data-guide-pose="quiet" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><div class="limits-list"><details data-reveal><summary>It does not learn from every message.<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Only replies saved by a moderator are reused.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>When the rules change, update the saved answer.<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Edit or remove the saved guidance. Future questions use the current facts. The bot does not broadcast corrections into old threads.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>The model can still get things wrong.<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Replies include their source so a person can check them. Unsupported questions wait. An account or payment issue needs private human support.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>You run the bot and choose the model.<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Use local Ollama inference, or Paper Instruments for replies with local embeddings. You also choose the database, support channels, and moderators.</p></details></div></section>

  <section class="project-note wrap" data-reveal><div><p class="project-note__text">I built this after seeing the same support questions in the MLH Discord.</p><div class="guide-stop origin-guide-stop" data-guide-stop="origin" data-guide-pose="idle" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="project-note__after">Different people needed the same information, but the useful answer was buried in another thread.<br /><br />Made for the <a href="https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week3-2026-10-19" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge: Week 3</a> on DEV. The theme is Slow and Steady: build something that does the work so you don't have to. This is a hackathon project, so expect rough edges.</p></section>

  <section class="setup-section" id="use"><div class="wrap setup-section__inner"><div class="setup-section__copy" data-reveal><h2>Run it in Discord.</h2><p>A Discord bot token. MongoDB.<br />Ollama or a Paper Instruments key.</p><a class="setup-link" href="/setup/"><span>Setup instructions</span><span class="setup-link__arrow"><img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="22" height="22" alt="" /></span></a><div class="guide-stop setup-guide-stop" data-guide-stop="setup" data-guide-pose="sleep" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><div class="setup-steps" data-reveal><ol class="setup-order"><li>Create your Discord application.</li><li>Add the environment values and start the bot.</li><li>Connect a forum. Save the first useful reply.</li></ol><div class="source-links"><a href="https://github.com/sea-deep/threadsherpa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub <img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" /></a><a href="https://gitlab.com/wdipak/threadsherpa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitLab <img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" /></a><a href="https://github.com/sea-deep/threadsherpa/blob/main/docs/SETUP.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quick start <img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" /></a></div></div></div></section>
  <script>import '../scripts/afterlife';</script>
</Base>
